FINAL LESSON — THE AFRICAN AI GOVERNANCE MINDSET
The most important principle across all four modules is:
Do not build AI first and ask governance questions later. Build governance into the AI system from the beginning.

A mature African AI system should therefore be designed across eight dimensions:

1. Legal
Is the system lawful?

2. Data
Is the data appropriately collected, processed and protected?

3. Technical
Is the architecture secure and resilient?

4. Sovereignty
Does the institution retain appropriate control over its data and AI infrastructure?

5. Fairness
Could the system produce unjustified unequal outcomes?

6. Human oversight
Can humans understand, challenge and override consequential decisions?

7. Accountability
Who is responsible when the system fails?

8. Transparency
Can stakeholders understand how AI is being used?

